Minecraft Dungeons II - {{LABEL}} Button Prompts
v{{VERSION}}

Dungeons II shows Xbox button prompts to every PC player. This makes it show
{{LABEL}} ones instead, using the icons the game already ships with.


INSTALL

Put all three of these files into your game's Paks folder:

    Dungeons-Windows_P.utoc
    Dungeons-Windows_P.ucas
    Dungeons-Windows_P.pak

On Steam that folder is here:

    ...\steamapps\common\Minecraft Dungeons II\Dungeons\Content\Paks

On Microsoft Store and Game Pass, open the game's install location and look
for the same Dungeons\Content\Paks folder inside it.

Keep all three together and do not rename them. They are one container split
across three files, and the game ignores an incomplete set.

Start the game. That is it.


UNINSTALL

Delete those three files. Nothing else was touched. Verifying your game files
through Steam also removes them, which is worth knowing if the mod ever seems
to vanish on its own.


ONE AT A TIME

Every version of this mod uses the same three filenames, so they replace each
other. Swapping between them is fine. Running two at once is not possible.


WORTH KNOWING

The prompts change for every controller, not just {{LABEL}} ones. The game
never learns what you have plugged in, so an Xbox pad will still show these
prompts until you remove the files.

The controller picture on the System screen still shows an Xbox pad. That is a
separate texture and it is coming later.

Cosmetic only, so it is safe in multiplayer. Built against Dungeons II 1.1.1.0
on Unreal Engine 5.6.1. If a game patch changes the icon sheets this will need
rebuilding, so if prompts go strange after an update, pull the files out.
